The Day 222 assessment is written and committed (2d7122ab) at session_plan/assessment.md. I didn't re-run the full test suite, as instructed.

Where things stand:
• **Health:** the last 4 evolve runs succeeded, CI is green and there were no reverts.
• **Recent work:** all three Day 221 sessions went 2/2. They continued the --deny-dir work (#1002) and the "says it failed but exits 0" commands (#982).
• **Upstream:** yoagent#260, which I filed last night, was closed and fixed upstream at 01:30Z. The fix isn't in a published release yet.

What I found today:
1. **Upgrading yoagent naively would bring back the Day 219 loss.** 0.24.3 is out and fixes a lot: MCP over stdio, streams that fail but come back looking finished, cancel markers, and searches that now keep partial matches. But it also starts retrying "Overloaded" inside yoagent itself. That retry goes through handle_provider_retry (src/prompt.rs:981), which deliberately ignores the retry_after_partial opt-in from #997. So a plain cargo update -p yoagent would let one Overloaded error abort an evolve task again and lose its work. The upgrade has to settle that door's policy in the same task, together with #991.
2. **Claude Haiku 5.5 (claude-haiku-5-5) is unknown to yoyo and priced wrong.** `cost.rs:121` charges it at old Haiku 3.5 prices, about 8× too high. It also gets a generic 200K context setting instead of 1M. The $0.10/$0.50 price comes from Claude Code's changelog, so it needs checking against Anthropic's pricing page before anyone encodes it.
3. **@path mentions and /add skip the --deny-dir check (I found this by reading the code, not by running it).** `read_file_for_add` is a plain file read, and neither caller passes the directory restrictions. That's another door #1002 doesn't list yet. Claude Code just started applying its deny rules to @-mentions.
4. **The #982 leftovers are confirmed live:** def and outline with nothing found, bare run, and tree --bogus all exit 0.
5. **`yoyo refs has no shell command, so it falls through to a paid model turn.** yoyo def` does have one.

Not measured:
• **Skill folders under --deny-dir:** still unmeasured. `--print-system-prompt` can't show skills, and a skill that links outside the project is already refused. The case still open is a skill linked into a denied folder inside the project.
• **Two Claude Code fixes I haven't checked yoyo against:** MCP tools with invalid names (CC now skips names over 128 characters, which made every request fail), and <system-reminder> tags in hook output.

Side notes:
• Two of my probes (yoyo refs, yoyo symbols) went to the model and cost a small amount.
• I saved the Claude Code and yoagent changes to yopedia.
